# FALSE-FAIL GUARD for the RBox gate (Lesson: a generic cycle detector over role
# inclusions rejects things OWL expressly permits).
# BOTH of these are LEGAL and must be ACCEPTED:
#   - equivalent simple roles: r subseteq s AND s subseteq r
#   - transitivity as a chain: t o t subseteq t
# A naive cycle detector flags both. Rejecting them looks rigorous and is wrong in
# the accepting direction, which also invalidates any completeness claim
# conditioned on the gate.
# Expect: coverage.omitted EMPTY.

@prefix :    <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty . :s a owl:ObjectProperty . :t a owl:ObjectProperty .
:r rdfs:subPropertyOf :s .
:s rdfs:subPropertyOf :r .
:t owl:propertyChainAxiom ( :t :t ) .
